From 5b6a259017d5c5a500f368850802cab08b7cb221 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 09:16:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 37/42] transports: align tenant handler response shapes with
 legacy + UI contracts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to patch 0034 (tenant_providers shape fixes). Same class
of bug — tenant-scoped admin handlers were returning custom
envelopes that diverged from the legacy /api/<entity> shapes the
UI's RTK Query mutations + optimistic cache updates were built
against. The provider fixes worked end-to-end in browser testing,
which made the sibling handlers' divergence visible — every other
tenant-scoped entity was at risk of the same React-error-boundary
"Something went wrong" toast plus silently empty admin pages.

Five files, same pattern:

  - List GET now returns {<entities>, count, total_count, limit,
    offset} matching the legacy ListXxxResponse contract; the
    previous {tenant_id, <entities>, total} envelope made
    RTK Query's typed `draft.<entities>` undefined under the
    UI's getXxx query type, so admin pages rendered zero rows
    even when the DB held rows.

  - Create POST now returns {message, <entity>} for teams,
    customers, budgets, rate_limits (matches legacy /api/governance
    POSTs). VK gets the same shape; MCP create returns the
    {status, message} variant that mcpApi.ts types as
    CreateMCPClientResponse.

  - GET single now wraps as {<entity>: object} for VK, MCP,
    teams, customers, budgets, rate_limits — matches the legacy
    getXxx query return types.

  - PUT update now returns {message, <entity>} (or {status, message}
    for MCP) matching the optimistic-update shape.

  - DELETE used to return 204 No Content; legacy returns 200 +
    {message: string}. RTK Query tolerates either, but the UI's
    deleteXxx mutation is typed as {message: string} and shows
    that text in a toast on success. Aligning the contract keeps
    the toast meaningful and avoids the type-narrowing dead-code.

Handler files:
  - tenant_virtualkeys.go
  - tenant_mcp.go
  - tenant_teams.go
  - tenant_customers.go
  - tenant_governance_misc.go (budgets + rate_limits)

Test files updated to assert the new shapes — every list test
swaps .Total → .Count, every DELETE test swaps StatusNoContent →
StatusOK, the VK create test reads from the new {message,
virtual_key} envelope. mt_integration_test.go follows for the VK
list + MCP delete it asserts against.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
